  "question": {
    "text": "The set of all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> in the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> for which the points<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lie&nbsp;on the same side of the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is?",
